  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - .",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces shall be as in drawing numbers 4620 RRP4620-05-S-001, 4620 RRP4620-05-E-001 and 4620 RRP4620-05-E002 received 5.10.04 unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority (before the building is used).",
    "Condition : 5 - No fans, louvres, ducts or other external plant shall be installed without the prior approval of the Local Planning Authority",
    "Condition : 6 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 7am to 7pm Mondays to Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority",
    "Condition : 7 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approval by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n(iv)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n(v)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n(vi)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on tot eh adjoining properties\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for the storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied",
    "Condition : 9 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and these works shall be carried out as approved. These details shall include proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing material.\r\nSoft landscape works shall include planting plans; written specifications; schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme.\r\n",
    "Condition : 10 - The premises shall be used for retail/restaurant use only within the Use Class Order 1995 and no individual retail/restaurant units is to be greater than 600 sqm",
    "Condition : 11 - Prior to first opening of the A1 or A3 Use, details of the servicing operation, including hours of servicing, numbers of deliveries, access to the service yard etc shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. The scheme so approved shall be fully implemented"
  ],
